-- Q3385: Internal-Use Software and Cloud Computing [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Apply ASC 350-40 for internal-use software regardless of marketing plans","Use neither standard since dual-purpose software has no specific guidance","Choose whichever standard produces the more favorable capitalization outcome","Apply ASC 985-20 once technological feasibility is established for external sale"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): When software is developed for both internal use and external sale, ASC 985-20 (software to be sold) takes precedence once a detailed program design or working model establishes technological feasibility. The external marketing plan triggers this standard''s capitalization criteria. Wrong (A): ASC 350-40 applies only when there is no substantive plan to market the software externally. Wrong (B): Dual-purpose software does have specific guidance; ASC 985-20 governs when external sale is planned. Wrong (C): Entities cannot elect between the two standards; the applicable guidance depends on the software''s intended use.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3385;

-- Q3387: Internal-Use Software and Cloud Computing [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["An operating expense recognized ratably over the hosting term","An intangible asset, with hosting services expensed separately","A right-of-use asset classified under the ASC 842 lease guidance","A prepaid expense amortized over the full contract period"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 350-40, when a cloud hosting arrangement contains a software license element that the customer can take possession of and run independently, the license is recognized as an intangible asset. The remaining hosting service portion is expensed as a service contract over the hosting term. Wrong (A): Expensing the entire arrangement ignores the separable license element that qualifies for capitalization. Wrong (C): ASC 842 applies to leases of tangible assets, not software license elements within hosting arrangements. Wrong (D): Treating the license as a prepaid expense fails to recognize it as a distinct intangible asset under ASC 350-40.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3387;

-- Q3388: Advanced Lease Transactions [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Use any asset for any period without restrictions on direction","Purchase an asset at a discount from the owner at term end","Control the use of an identified asset for a specified period","Receive ongoing maintenance services from an asset''s owner"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 842-10-15-2, a lease exists when a contract conveys the right to control the use of an identified asset for a period of time in exchange for consideration. Control requires the right to obtain substantially all economic benefits and direct the asset''s use. Wrong (A): Merely using an asset without control over its direction does not meet the lease definition under ASC 842. Wrong (B): A purchase option is not the defining characteristic of a lease; leases convey use rights, not ownership. Wrong (D): Service arrangements where the supplier directs the asset''s use do not qualify as leases.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3388;

-- Q3389: Advanced Lease Transactions [medium/L2]
