  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 805-10-25-10, in a step acquisition the acquirer remeasures its previously held equity interest at acquisition-date fair value. Any gain or loss is recognized in earnings in the period control is obtained, and the full combination is accounted for using the acquisition method. Wrong (A): Historical cost does not reflect the current value of the interest at the date control is achieved. Wrong (B): Book value from the investee''s statements may differ from fair value and is not the required measurement basis. Wrong (D): The original purchase price is superseded by the fair value remeasurement requirement at the acquisition date.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3421;

-- Q3423: Derivatives and Hedging [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["An interest rate derivative only, modifying the rate structure","A commodity derivative based on the currency exchange element","Both a foreign currency and an interest rate derivative combined","An equity derivative linked to the underlying debt instruments"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 815, a cross-currency interest rate swap exchanges both the currency denomination and interest rate type (USD fixed to EUR floating), creating two distinct risk components: foreign currency risk and interest rate risk. It is classified as both derivative types. Wrong (A): Classifying it solely as an interest rate derivative ignores the currency exchange component from USD to EUR. Wrong (B): Currency swaps are foreign currency derivatives, not commodity derivatives; currencies are not commodities under ASC 815. Wrong (D): The swap modifies debt terms but does not derive value from equity instruments.$EXPL$
