  choices = $EXPL$["Capitalize all $75,000 as application development stage costs","Capitalize the $25,000 purging costs and expense the $50,000 routines","Expense all $75,000 as period costs when incurred during migration","Capitalize the $50,000 conversion routines and expense the $25,000 purging"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 350-40 as extended by ASU 2018-15, building and testing automated data conversion programs may be capitalized during the application development stage. However, data purging and cleansing activities are expensed as incurred because they do not add functionality. Wrong (A): Data purging costs ($25,000) do not qualify for capitalization under ASU 2018-15 and must be expensed. Wrong (B): This reverses the correct treatment; conversion routines are capitalizable while purging is not. Wrong (C): Blanket expensing ignores that conversion routine development qualifies for capitalization during the application development stage.$EXPL$
