  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 805-20-25-4, IPR&D acquired in a business combination is recognized at fair value as an indefinite-lived intangible asset. It is not amortized but tested for impairment until the project is completed (then reclassified as finite-lived and amortized) or abandoned (then written off). Wrong (A): Post-2009 guidance under ASC 805 requires capitalization of acquired IPR&D rather than immediate expensing. Wrong (B): IPR&D is classified as indefinite-lived while in process; amortization begins only after project completion. Wrong (C): ASC 805 requires measurement at acquisition-date fair value, not the acquiree''s historical carrying amount.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4832;

-- Q4839: Business Combinations [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
