  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 805-20-30-1, most assets and liabilities are measured at fair value, but employee benefit obligations are an exception. They are measured per ASC 715 using actuarial methods rather than acquisition-date fair value, along with income taxes (ASC 740) and certain lease obligations. Wrong (A): Accounts payable are measured at fair value under the general ASC 805 principle with no specific exception. Wrong (B): Contingent liabilities are measured at acquisition-date fair value under ASC 805 and are not an exception. Wrong (D): Long-term debt is measured at fair value under the general rule and does not receive special measurement treatment.$EXPL$
